`--week` and `--listen` options), and p13-scope.py (the scope guard).

The cross-correlation helper of the cut probe: the first run of the probe printed max-ncc values over
1. The cause was my own edit of the product of the spectra: the correct product is conj(A) * B, with
the real part ar*br + ai*bi and the imaginary part ar*bi - ai*br, the form of the Phase 12 helper and
of the library function `looksLikeCut`. A scratch script compared the helper with a brute-force
correlation on a synthetic cut: the correct form gives 1.000 at the true lag, the wrong form gives
0.230. The probe was corrected and re-run; the control gives 1.000 and every clip gives at most
0.221, far under the 0.98 line.

